## DotnetOptions

**Namespace:** `Cyrena.Dotnet.Options`
**Assembly:** `Cyrena.Dotnet`

### Purpose
Constants for .NET development configuration keys and builder IDs.

### Constants

```csharp
public class DotnetOptions
{
    public const string SolutionFilePath = "sln-path";
    public const string LastProject = "sln.last_proj";

    public const string CsClassLibrary = "cs-class-library";
    public const string CsBlazorLibrary = "cs-blazor-lib";
    public const string CsBlazorApp = "cs-blazor-app";
    public const string CsMvcApp = "cs-mvc-app";
    public const string CsMvcLib = "cs-mvc-lib";

    public const string ProjectFilePath = "proj.path";

    public class CSharp
    {
        public const string Namespace = "namespace";
        public const string TargetFrameworks = "target_frameworks";
    }
}
```

### Builder IDs
These map to `ICodeBuilder.Id` values:
- `".net-solution"` — SolutionBuilder (not listed here, used by DotnetShortcut)
- `"cs-class-library"` — ClassLibrarySolutionBuilder
- `"cs-blazor-lib"` — BlazorLibrarySolutionsBuilder
- `"cs-blazor-app"` — BlazorAppSolutionBuilder
- `"cs-mvc-app"` — MvcAppSolutionBuilder
- `"cs-mvc-lib"` — MvcLibrarySolutionBuilder

### Configuration Keys
- `SolutionFilePath` — Path to .sln or .slnx file
- `LastProject` — ID of currently active project (persisted in config)
- `ProjectFilePath` — Path to individual .csproj file
- `CSharp.Namespace` — Root namespace
- `CSharp.TargetFrameworks` — Target framework string
